<spell-notebook "terms usage">
	<header level="1">
		Terms
		<header>Terms list facts as a label and a value each, lined up.</>
	</>
	<terms-tab-bar showing="usage"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#using-it">Using it</>
				<ui-item link="#accessibility">Accessibility</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- USAGE:  how to use it (attributes in practice, events, framework snippets), keyboard, accessibility. -->
	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			`<ui-terms>` lists facts, a label and a value each:  HTML's `<dl>`, `<dt>` and `<dd>`.

			- `<ui-term label="Suit" value="hearts">`:  the label and value as attributes.
			- Or written inside:  the value as the term's content, the label in `slot="label"`, for anything more than text.
			- The labels line up in one column and the values in the next.
			- `direction="horizontal"` puts the terms side by side, wrapping.
			- `spacing` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) is the space between terms.
			- A `<ui-term>` on its own draws its label and value on one line.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>Screen readers hear each label as a term and its value as the term's definition (`role="term"`, `role="definition"`).</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
